# L §4.5 Whatever a version states is read as its rows are (tally 2.1.8 R12, B6): st, known in a window that holds the
# cut 2026-04-10, states bank[r1] fulfilling pay[2026-03]. Seen, the row stands for the instance; unseen, the instance:
# one movement either way, so March's count is 1 (k1); flows(pay) differs, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the row and its
# version (k2); next(transfers, 2026-03-01) is that hole, the row's day (03-03) and the plan's (03-01) differing, never
# RUN-TIE (n1). 2.1.7's refcore named the row alone and gave next the row's day.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-05-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input lvl: num

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  lvl = 0 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-20)
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 7.00 PLN, fulfils: pay[2026-03]) "r"

ask k1: count(t in transfers over 2026-03) as known 2026-04-10
ask k2: flows(pay, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-10
ask n1: next(transfers, 2026-03-01).day as known 2026-04-10
=== expect
k1: 1
  cut 2026-04-10
k2: ?"date within window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-20) not precise enough for the cut 2026-04-10" (bank[r1], st)
  cut 2026-04-10
n1: ?"date within window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-20) not precise enough for the cut 2026-04-10" (bank[r1], st)
  cut 2026-04-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD input lvl is read by nothing
